WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.769
Jesse, right now you have
four wins under your belt.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.337 line:8%
You've got $20,000
in your pocket.

00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:07.107 line:8%
You're fighting
for the five grand.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.542 line:8%
But being that this is your
fifth competition, if you win,

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:12.012 line:8%
you will also receive
that bonus of $10,000.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.913
Do you want to pick the
weapon, or do you want to pick

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.749
the forge welding technique?

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:18.050
I want the weapon.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.919
All right, what
are you thinking?

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.755
I'm thinking the
pair of pugio daggers.

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:26.793
Holy cow, what a bold choice.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:30.596
Pugio was a popular sidearm in
second and third century Rome.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.565
Gladiators were known
to battle with two

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.100
pugio, one in each hand.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.835
These close quarter
combat weapons

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.403
featured a wide
leaf-shaped blade

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.105
to inflict deep lethal
wounds upon an enemy,

00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:42.375
both on the battlefield
and inside the walls

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.609
of the Colosseum.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.911
However, the pugio is most
well known as the weapon

00:00:46.011 --> 00:00:48.114
used to murder Julius Caesar.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.348
John, you've got
a choice to make.

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:50.883
What forge welding
technique do you want

00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:52.351
to use to build your daggers?

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:55.221
Let's go with canister, and
we're going to have to use

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.689
some bicycle chain in it.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.059
Bicycle chain in
canister Damascus.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.694
All right, very, very tall
order on the plate today.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:02.761
So good luck, stay sharp.

00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:05.297
Your time starts now.

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:06.832
Because this is
my fifth battle,

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.501
I'm definitely a
little bit tired.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.770
I've hit that bottom
plateau in terms of energy,

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:12.404
and the only way I can go is up.

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:14.006
I used to forge out
chef's knives at home

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.308
in batches of two or three.

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:18.477
So this is a pretty
comfortable zone for me.

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:20.947
I think my canister is
up to temperature now.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.448
I think it's the
perfect time to bring

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.751
them over to the squaring dies
and start setting those wells.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.151
Right now, I have
them all forged

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:27.653
to shape, fit to dimension.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.890
Just want to get them
ready for heat treat now.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.391
It's time for le quench.

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:35.160
So I decide to do one at a time.

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:37.030
Oh, we've got a quench.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.231
The temperature of my
first blade looked perfect.

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:43.402
Now, it's time to put
blade two in the fire.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:46.005
All right, Jesse's
got two blades quenched.

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:47.173
It went perfectly.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.540
There were no warps
in either blade.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.643
It's time to grind these
blades to final dimension.

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:54.146
I slap on a fresh 36 grit
and just start going ham.

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:55.314
But there's still
a few things that I

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.716
need to do in this
round, include

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.617
finish shaping the handle
and then sharpening it.

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:00.653
I leave myself a lot of time
to sharpen these blades,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.022
because I don't want
to run out of time

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:05.358
and have one edge unsharpened.

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:09.161
So the idea that I've got is
that I'm going to forge the two

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:11.297
knives out of one billet,
and I'm going to stretch

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.633
out the tang in the middle.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.601
And I'll cut those in two.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:19.139
So after I've got them ground,
now it's time to heat treat.

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:25.144
Out of the oil, it looks good.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:26.845
I think I've got what I want.

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:28.247
That's going to work.

00:02:28.313 --> 00:02:30.283
And then I go to the grinder.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:37.489 line:8%
The second blade I noticed
a delam on the edge.

00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:39.725 line:8%
I am concerned that another
could show up while I grind.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.995 line:8%
But I think I've still
got enough width,

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.730 line:8%
and so now, I'm just
going to work that out.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.433
I now have to assemble
these two handles.

00:02:47.499 --> 00:02:50.069
It is going to be a big
challenge all the way around.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:53.973
I know I have to find a handle,
because the clock marches on.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.975
Everything seems
to be just right,

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.344
but I glance, and
I'm seeing I've

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.346
used up better than an hour.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:03.816
So I know I've got
to keep moving on.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.051
It's a very complex handle.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.319
I know that I have a lot
of moving parts in this.

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:09.121
I know I'm going to have
to make sure everything

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:10.857
fits properly with it.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:13.259
What John's doing
is a great idea,

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.561
but it's very, very
time consuming.

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:19.398
It's not an easy process,
but I do get them inset some.

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:24.503
After I get the pommel glued
on, then it's to the grinder.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.305
It looks like a
potato on a stick.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.606
It doesn't look great.

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:30.176
And I need to get this
shaped into something

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.711
that is functional.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:33.512
What John's got going on in
his handle, it kind of almost

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.247
looks like a dog chew bone.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.483
I still need to
sharpen the blade.

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.484
I get it etched.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.219
I'm racing the clock right now.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.754
And I don't have time
to make mistakes today.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:47.493
5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:49.796
Bladesmiths, turn off your
machines, put down your tools.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.430
This battle is over.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.298
Bladesmiths, welcome
to our strength test.

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:55.768
The armor, stab, and slash.

00:03:58.738 --> 00:03:59.638
Jesse, you're up first.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:00.772
You ready to go?

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:01.874
I'm ready to go.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.343
I know you love going first.

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:04.510
Yep.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:10.783
[suspenseful music]

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.708
All right, Jesse,
you survived.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.242
Good job.

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:38.377
Your blades look great.

00:04:38.443 --> 00:04:41.446
I like the symmetry on these.

00:04:41.546 --> 00:04:43.082
They look like a matched pair.

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:44.083
Everything's tight.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.184
Everything's smooth.

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:47.520
Your edges are still good.

00:04:47.586 --> 00:04:51.390
You do have a few flat spots,
but there's not enough there

00:04:51.456 --> 00:04:53.492
where I can catch a nail on it.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:57.030
The biggest issue I
have is the handles.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.165
They have no grip
to them whatsoever,

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.933
enough so that, with
one of the chops,

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.168
I actually caught a knuckle.

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:04.203
It was a knuckle slip up.

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:05.438
Some contouring would
have made it a lot

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:06.773
easier to hold on to them.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:09.575
But otherwise, great job.

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:10.742
Thank you.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.378
It's always fun being the
second guy, right, John?

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.246
Sure, why not?

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:15.848
- You ready to go?
- Absolutely.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:16.916
All right, let's do it.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.857
[suspenseful music]

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:47.512
All right, John, you survived.

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:49.215
Got to be happy about that.

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:51.050
You've got some
glinting on the edges,

00:05:51.116 --> 00:05:52.985
nothing I'm really catching on.

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:55.788
The biggest problem I have,
the contouring you have

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:59.058
on there is basically
the exact opposite

00:05:59.124 --> 00:06:00.459
of what I said about Jesse's.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:02.595
They're not sliding
anywhere, but

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:04.364
they're not comfortable at all.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:08.400
But, overall, they held
together and nothing came loose.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.769
Edges survived.
Good job.

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:10.870
Thank you.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.609
That handled the forge.

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:19.645
This is the sharpness
test, the banner slice.

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:23.182
Jesse, you're up first.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.283
Are you ready for this?

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:25.284
I'm ready.

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:26.785
All right.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:28.521
[choral music]

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:48.674
All right, Jesse, let's talk
about your matching pugio

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:49.574
daggers here.

00:06:49.674 --> 00:06:50.910
That's a beautiful matched set.

00:06:50.976 --> 00:06:53.579
They're quite identical,
very close to that.

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:56.082
Now, your edge, your
edges cut nicely,

00:06:56.149 --> 00:07:00.486
and overall, your
weapon will cut.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.054
John, your turn, sir.
Are you ready?

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:03.556
- Yes sir.
- Let's do this.

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:14.834
[suspenseful music]

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:28.113
All right, John, let's talk
about your pugio daggers here.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.682
Your edges are sharp.

00:07:29.748 --> 00:07:32.051
It's just that it's got a grind
here that's not razor sharp.

00:07:32.117 --> 00:07:34.419
So when cutting with this, there
are some areas in this where

00:07:34.486 --> 00:07:36.621
it just got snagged
with the blade,

00:07:36.721 --> 00:07:38.824
and it does rip a little bit.

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:41.894
But overall, sir, your
pugio daggers will cut.

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:42.995
Thank you.

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.801
All right, gentlemen, after
eight hours of furious battle

00:07:49.901 --> 00:07:51.670
where you guys built
your pugio daggers out

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.739
of bicycle chain
canister Damascus,

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.841
it is coming down
to a final decision.

00:07:55.907 --> 00:07:57.643
Only one of you can
come out of here on top

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.011
with the title of
Gladiator of the Forge.

00:07:59.078 --> 00:08:01.780
Jesse, if you win, that
will be your fifth win,

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:05.485
and you will have
$35,000 in your pocket.

00:08:05.551 --> 00:08:08.420
Now, John, if you win, you'll
stop his winning streak,

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:09.989
get your first Gladiator
of the Forge title,

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:12.324
a check for $5,000, and
the opportunity to go

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:14.760
forward into the next battle.

00:08:14.826 --> 00:08:16.328
Our judges have
discussed your blades,

00:08:16.394 --> 00:08:18.664
and they made a final decision.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:20.233
Today's Gladiator
of the Forge is--

00:08:25.738 --> 00:08:26.438
Jesse.

00:08:26.538 --> 00:08:27.472
You have done it again.

00:08:27.539 --> 00:08:29.342
That is five total wins.

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:31.377
John, you brought us
a good pair of blades,

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:33.079
but unfortunately, they
didn't come out on top.

00:08:33.179 --> 00:08:35.314
And Jay is going
to tell you why.

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:37.416
John, you did a
great job out there.

00:08:37.516 --> 00:08:38.817
You should be definitely
proud of yourself.

00:08:38.884 --> 00:08:40.852
We sure as heck enjoyed
watching you work.

00:08:40.919 --> 00:08:44.123
But at the end of the day,
the inner grinds on your pugio

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:46.759
daggers weren't as sharp
as your competitor's, as we

00:08:46.825 --> 00:08:48.560
saw during the sharpness test.

00:08:48.627 --> 00:08:51.430
And you had a great
idea for the handle,

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:52.665
but it kind of went south.

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:54.866
So that's why we're
sending you home.

00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:56.669
John, there's no
question you're talented.

00:08:56.736 --> 00:08:59.004
I know you had your competitor
here worried for a little bit.

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:00.706
Unfortunately, you didn't
come out on top today.

00:09:00.773 --> 00:09:02.541
At this point, I'm going to
have to ask you to please

00:09:02.641 --> 00:09:03.776
step off the forge floor.

00:09:03.842 --> 00:09:05.644
This is just one more
learning experience.

00:09:05.744 --> 00:09:07.479
Take your education and
move to the next thing.

00:09:07.579 --> 00:09:09.915
Jesse, you are a
five-time champion.

00:09:10.015 --> 00:09:13.585
You got another check for five
grand and a bonus of $10,000.

00:09:13.685 --> 00:09:15.121 line:8%
Congratulations.
- Thank you.

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:16.321 line:14%
[applause]

00:09:16.422 --> 00:09:18.257 line:8%
So right now, I
got to ask again,

00:09:18.324 --> 00:09:21.159
do you have enough energy
to go back in the forge

00:09:21.259 --> 00:09:22.461
and fight out another battle?

00:09:22.527 --> 00:09:24.096
Put me in, coach.

00:09:24.196 --> 00:09:25.096
I love it.

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:26.098
All right, man.

00:09:26.165 --> 00:09:27.433
I have five titles.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.970
I'm not ready to give up
this seat any time soon.

